# ghostopia — example environment.
#
# Copy this file to `.env`, fill in the four required values below, then run `make run`.
# ghostopia is a thin program on top of GhostCrawl: GhostCrawl does all the browsing and
# scraping work; ghostopia points a workforce at your targets and shows the results. The
# server reads this file at boot; the browser UI never sees any of these values.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # edit .env
#   make run
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — the four values you must set
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your GhostCrawl key / license key. This is the credential ghostopia uses to run work
# through GhostCrawl. It stays on the server and is never sent to the browser.
GHOSTOPIA_GC_TOKEN=

# The GhostCrawl endpoint ghostopia talks to.
#   NOTE: enter the LOCAL PORT if you run GhostCrawl yourself (Docker / self-host) —
#         e.g. http://localhost:8080
#         OR the GhostCrawl CLOUD endpoint if you use GhostCrawl cloud —
#         e.g. https://api.ghostcrawl.io
GHOSTOPIA_GC_BASE_URL=https://api.ghostcrawl.io

# The signing secret the server uses to mint the short-lived token the UI authenticates
# with. Use any long random string (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`). Keep it private.
GHOSTOPIA_JWT_SECRET=

# Where the local results database (SQLite) lives. The best-price / detail findings the
# workforce brings back are saved here. A relative path is fine.
GHOSTOPIA_DB_PATH=ghostopia.sqlite

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — sensible defaults; set only if you want to change behavior
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OPTIONAL bring-your-own extraction model. You do NOT need this — GhostCrawl is the all-in-one:
# every department (books AND the advanced real-retail Spooky Masks / Costumes) pulls the FULL
# priced product list from a store's listing via GhostCrawl's OWN native structured extraction
# (schema.org JSON-LD / microdata / Open Graph) — no model, no third party, no per-site rules.
# Set a key here ONLY to add your own model as an enhancement for pages that carry no
# machine-readable product data; leave blank (the default) to run fully on GhostCrawl.
# GHOSTOPIA_BYO_EXTRACT_KEY=
# Model provider type: anthropic (default) | openai | openai_compat | google.
# GHOSTOPIA_BYO_EXTRACT_TYPE=anthropic
# Model id (defaults per type — anthropic: claude-sonnet-4-5, openai: gpt-4o-mini,
# google: gemini-2.0-flash).
# GHOSTOPIA_BYO_EXTRACT_MODEL=
# Base URL — required only for the openai / openai_compat types.
# GHOSTOPIA_BYO_EXTRACT_BASE_URL=

# Bring-your-own LLM key for the agent path (used only when you opt into a model-backed
# agent). Read server-side only. Leave blank for the deterministic default.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Which GhostCrawl browser engine the app opens sessions with (default: chrome). The
# live browser view is captured on chrome sessions.
# GHOSTOPIA_ENGINE=chrome

# Advanced: a full JSON map of named GhostCrawl targets, e.g.
#   {"cloud": {"base_url": "https://api.ghostcrawl.io", "token_ref": "GHOSTOPIA_GC_TOKEN"}}
# When unset, a single "cloud" target is synthesized from GHOSTOPIA_GC_BASE_URL +
# GHOSTOPIA_GC_TOKEN above — you do not need this for a one-endpoint setup.
# GHOSTOPIA_TARGETS=

# Where runtime-authored departments (targets you create in the UI) are persisted, so your
# own targets survive a restart. Defaults next to the database.
# GHOSTOPIA_AUTHORED_SECTIONS_PATH=

# Where a customized world map is loaded from (defaults to the shipped map).
# GHOSTOPIA_MAP_PATH=

# Where the built web UI is served from (defaults to apps/web/dist, which `make run` builds).
# GHOSTOPIA_WEB_DIST=

# Tuning knobs (positive integers). Defaults are chosen for a typical plan; shrink them for
# a small plan or raise them to fill a larger one.
#   GHOSTOPIA_GHOSTS_PER_SECTION      ghosts staffed per department (default 3)
#   GHOSTOPIA_LIVE_BROWSER_GHOSTS     watchable live-browser ghosts (default 2)
#   GHOSTOPIA_WORKFORCE_MAX_CONCURRENT forces the concurrent-work cap when set
#   GHOSTOPIA_IDLE_TEARDOWN_GRACE_S   seconds an idle world lingers before teardown
# GHOSTOPIA_GHOSTS_PER_SECTION=3
# GHOSTOPIA_LIVE_BROWSER_GHOSTS=2
# GHOSTOPIA_WORKFORCE_MAX_CONCURRENT=
# GHOSTOPIA_IDLE_TEARDOWN_GRACE_S=
